{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>All the days of the earth, etc. shall not cease.</b> These six seasons are two months each, as we learned: half of Tishrei and Marcheshvan and half of Kislev — seed; half of Kislev and Tevet and half of Shevat — קֹר (חֹרֶף) (Bava Metzia 106a)." "<b>Cold.</b> Harsher than חֹרֶף." "<b>חֹרֶף.</b> The season for planting barley and quick-ripening legumes, and it is half of Shevat and Adar and half of Nisan." "<b>Harvest.</b> Half of Nisan and Iyar and half of Sivan." "<b>Summer.</b> Half of Sivan, Tammuz, and half of Av — the season for picking figs and drying them in the fields; and its name is קַיִץ, as in ״הַלֶּחֶם וְהַקַּיִץ לֶאֱכוֹל הַנְּעָרִים״ (II Samuel 16)." "<b>Heat.</b> It is the end of the solar season — half of Av and Elul and half of Tishrei — when the world is hottest. As we learned in tractate Yoma: שִׁלְהֵי קַיְיטָא קָשֵׁי מִקַּיְיטָא." "<b>And day and night shall not cease.</b> This implies that they did cease all the days of the Flood — the constellations did not function, and no distinction was recognizable between day and night (Bereshit Rabbah 25; 34)." "<b>Shall not cease.</b> All these shall never cease to function in their order."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:08.648460365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}